From 7277310deb1a5e8394c0c4c2a10349b58e48192a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Praveen Talari <praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 21:41:40 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] PENDING: spi: geni-qcom: Reconfigure SPI mode after system
 resume

The SPI GENI controller loses its hardware configuration across
system suspend and resume. However, the driver retains cached mode
and chip-select information and uses it to avoid redundant register
programming during subsequent transfers.

As a result, the first transfer after resume may skip reprogramming
SPI configuration registers even though the hardware state has been
lost, leaving the controller configured incorrectly.

Introduce a restore-needed flag and invalidate the cached
configuration during resume. Force SPI mode and chip-select
parameters to be reconfigured on the first transfer after resume,
ensuring that the controller state is restored before any data
transfer is initiated.

Fixes failures observed after system resume where SPI configuration
was not reapplied because the cached software state matched the
requested transfer parameters.

Change-Id: I13770c39e1ce9b87e345e0bdd96a3735d3a0705b
Signed-off-by: Praveen Talari <praveen.talari@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
index 5708c6dfa2d9..730afe7ddd57 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c
@@ -1462,7 +1462,15 @@ static int __maybe_unused spi_geni_resume(struct device *dev)
 	if (pm_suspend_target_state == PM_SUSPEND_MEM) {
 		dev_dbg(dev, "%s: In S2R\n", __func__);
 		mas->cur_xfer_mode = GENI_SE_INVALID;
+
+		/*
+		 * Initialize last_mode, last_cs and cur_bits_per_word to
+		 * 0, ~0U and 0	during system resume to force hardware
+		 * reconfiguration after DSQB.
+		 */
 		mas->last_mode = 0;
+		mas->last_cs = U8_MAX;
+		mas->cur_bits_per_word = 0;
 		ret = spi_geni_init(mas);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
-- 
